# The `test-viewer` tool (caos SPEC, "Tools"): run the static replay viewer's
# bundle inside the wasm runtime it will actually ship on.
#
# The docs are a HERE-STRING, so editing them re-keys this tool's arg tree and
# NOTHING it runs.
HELP=<<END
Build the replay-viewer bundle (via build-viewer) and RUN it: step three
fixture replays through the emitted wasm module under node, and run the client
band decode-failure regression. Returns a line per check and a pass/fail
banner.

This is the only thing that sees wasm32 bugs. Nim's `int` is 32 bits there and
the address space ends at 2 GB, so overflow checks trap on arithmetic that is
silently fine on 64-bit native and a big board exhausts memory — twice that
reached prod and every hosted replay hung on "WARMING UP" (PR #189). The native
suite cannot catch either.
@param [test-salt] Re-run the smokes while leaving the bundle build a cache hit — any fresh value re-keys the runs and nothing else.
END
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/imgtools --worker1:@=worker.sh --nim:@=DEEP-DEPS/nim --help=$HELP
